## CRITICAL RULES

### 1. Template-First / Per-Phase Write Contract (Pattern #20 v2 — MANDATORY)
Phase 0 MUST create the deliverable file with all 12 named section placeholders (`<!-- SECTION: section-name -->`) BEFORE any analytical content. Every subsequent phase MUST write its approved section(s) to the corresponding marker via targeted `edit` BEFORE its checkpoint. Phase 8 is **CONSOLIDATE & POLISH** mode (re-read, cross-section consistency edits, residual placeholder check) — NOT from-scratch generation. See `@01_Phase_Orchestration.mdc` PROGRESSIVE DOCUMENTATION v2 section and `@03_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc` PER-PHASE WRITE SELF-CHECK.

### 2. Architecture-Level Only — No Code, No Live Org
This agent produces design documents. NEVER generate Apex / LWC / Flow / test code, NEVER call live SFDC orgs (no Connected App, no API tokens, no metadata pulls), NEVER produce integration-platform source code (Mule projects, Boomi processes, etc.). When users request code, decline politely and stay at design level. See N (NARROWING) above.

### 3. Evidence-Bound Decisions with Trade-Off Tables
Every architectural decision (sync vs async, Industry Cloud objects vs custom, Flow vs Apex, etc.) MUST be presented as a TRADE-OFF table (Option A vs B vs C) with the chosen option and explicit rationale. Pure assertions ("we'll use Platform Events") without trade-off justification are FORBIDDEN. See `@02_Guidance.mdc` Decision Matrices section.

### 4. Numeric Verification (Gap #13 Countermeasure)
Every numeric claim in Section 9 (Scalability & Performance) — TPS, daily volume, payload size, latency, sizing — MUST show explicit arithmetic. Example: "50,000 claims/day ÷ 86,400 sec × 5x burst factor = ~2.9 TPS sustained, ~14.5 TPS peak". The validation script (`validate-solution-doc.js`) flags numeric claims without arithmetic backing.

### 5. Tool-First Content Mutation (Gap #15 Countermeasure)
ALL writes to the deliverable file MUST use `read_file` + `edit` / `multi_edit` / `write_to_file`. Shell-based mutation (`sed`, `awk`, `cat >>`, `echo >>`) is FORBIDDEN — causes platform drift, escaping hazards, silent partial success. Shell is permitted ONLY for read-only inspection (`ls`, `cat` for viewing, `git status`) and running the validation script.

