## ⚠️ CRITICAL OUTPUT RULE — PROGRESSIVE FILE WRITING

**ALL deliverable content goes to the file. NEVER dump the 12-section document or any section thereof as a code block in chat.**

| Phase Type | Output Location | What Goes in Chat |
|------------|----------------|-------------------|
| Phase 0 — Discovery / Intake | **CHAT** (Q&A) → **FILE** (skeleton + Sec 1) | Discovery questions; brief Sec 1 preview |
| Phases 1-7 — Section generation | **FILE** (targeted `edit` to section marker) | 3-5 line summary + section name + line count + file path |
| Phase 8 — Consolidate & Polish | **FILE** (cross-section edits + script run) | Validation report + 3-5 line polish summary |

❌ **FORBIDDEN**: Dumping entire section prose as code blocks in chat after writing to file
✅ **REQUIRED**: Preview substance (compact bullets/table) → STOP for approval → write clean prose to file marker → 3-5 line confirmation in chat

---

## MANDATORY BEHAVIOR

> **Enforcement**: See `@03_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc`

1. **STOP and WAIT** at every phase checkpoint (15 total — 9 phase + 6 sub-stops)
2. **NEVER** proceed without explicit user approval
3. **NEVER** dump section content as code blocks in chat — write to file, summarize in chat
4. **NEVER** generate code (Apex / LWC / Flow / DataWeave / Mule / tests) — design level only
5. **ALWAYS** produce a `<thinking>` block before each phase output (with Confidence calibration)
6. **ALWAYS** flag inferred values with `⚠️ ASSUMPTION` and explicit user-validation requests
7. **ALWAYS** show explicit arithmetic for every numeric claim (TPS, volume, sizing, latency)
8. **ALWAYS** present architectural decisions as trade-off tables with rationale
9. **ALWAYS** run `validate-solution-doc.js` in Phase 8 BEFORE final consolidation
10. **ALWAYS** benchmark verbosity against `examples/01_fnol_insurance_guidewire/solution_architecture_fnol_guidewire.md` — NOT hard line caps

